––– comment –––
PR #5060, https://bugzilla.altlinux.org/show_bug.cgi?id=61261: index_converter crashed with --config --all,
--path and --path --all, and --all skipped the first table. The crashes happened before any table file was read,
so tables with missing files are enough.
––– input –––
cat > /tmp/5060.conf <<'EOF'
index t1
{
    type = plain
    path = /tmp/5060/t1
}

index t2
{
    type = plain
    path = /tmp/5060/t2
}
EOF
––– output –––
––– input –––
index_converter --config /tmp/5060.conf --all 2>&1
––– output –––
using config file '/tmp/5060.conf'...
converting plain table 't1'
WARNING: failed to load table 't1', error: failed to open /tmp/5060/t1.sph: No such file or directory
converting plain table 't2'
WARNING: failed to load table 't2', error: failed to open /tmp/5060/t2.sph: No such file or directory
converted tables 0(2)
––– input –––
index_converter --path /tmp/5060/t1 2>&1
––– output –––
WARNING: unknown table type 't1'
converted tables 0(1)
––– input –––
index_converter --path . --all 2>&1 || true
––– output –––
FATAL: --all requires --config
